# The files every release of AerieOS carries, one a line, @VER@ the
# release's version (0.9.0, 0.9.0-dev.4501) and * as a shell pattern. The
# controller checks each release against the list at its own tag as its
# CI ends, and says on the bell what is missing and why, or that it is
# complete (releasefiles.py); the seal's last step publishes a dev build
# once it carries them all (seal-release.yml), and the release rehearsal
# says which were built (tools/release-missing.sh).
aerieos-controller-@VER@.tar.gz
aerieos-controller-@VER@.tar.gz.sha256
aerieos-companion-@VER@.exe
aerieos-companion-@VER@.exe.sha256
aerieos-usb-maker-@VER@.exe
aerieos-usb-maker-@VER@.exe.sha256
aerieos-companion-@VER@.pyz
aerieos-companion-@VER@.pyz.sha256
aerieos-vscode-@VER@.vsix
aerieos-vscode-@VER@.vsix.sha256
aerieos-app-@VER@.apk
aerieos-app-@VER@.apk.sha256
aerieos-os-@VER@.iso
aerieos-os-@VER@.iso.sha256
aerieos-os-@VER@.attestation.jsonl
aerieos-os-@VER@.stick.raw.xz
aerieos-os-@VER@.stick.raw.xz.sha256
# The container image this tag pushed, named by its digest, on one line:
# ghcr.io/aquilaelabs/aerieos@sha256:... The image carries no attestation
# and a registry's tag is whatever was last pushed under it; this file is
# in the signed list below, so a signed release says which image is its own.
aerieos-image-@VER@.digest
# The list of the files above with each one's sha256, and its signature
# (R199): what every install holds a file it takes to, so a release is not
# whole, and a dev build is not published, until it is signed
# (tools/release-sign.py: seal for a dev build, in seal-release.yml once the
# signed Android app is on the release; sign by the stable key's holder for
# a stable release).
SHA256SUMS
SHA256SUMS.sig
